committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1792133252 +0900

E1: program sets, --program-model/--program-temperature/--program-sample (prereg v4 block G-b)

HoldMem(program_writer=...): the D1s program requests of the definition
items (before and after the shift, plain and retraction-aware) go to that
client; every other request is the writer's. The E1 driver builds it only
off the defaults (another model, temperature != 0 or a sample index) and
only for runs with D1s cells, with extra_body from program_extra_body: the
model's default body (none for claude-* models, no thinking), the
temperature (replacing the body's 0.0) and memshift_sample=I (kept in the
cache key, removed before the HTTP request by the LLM client). The three
settings go into the manifest params (program_writer) and a non-default
model into the manifest models.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
